          %p
            %strong The case of S4 logic.
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            in a Kripke frame is (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive
            and)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitive
            but not necessarily
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"} symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S4+modal+logic"} S4 modal logic
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Kripke59"} Kripke 1959, §2
          %p
            In this case the relation no longer defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoid"}> setoid
            ”) as it does for the S5-case, but it defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-category"} (0,1)-category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            the elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %p
            As such, to retain the type-theoretic perspective
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BaseChange"} (3)
            in this case will require some form of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
